IMPORT prelude

-- ICA (Immigration & Checkpoints Authority, Singapore) -- a Singapore citizen's foreign spouse: the Long-Term Visit Pass,
-- permanent residence and citizenship, AS ICA PUBLISHES THEM.
--
-- SOURCES (all read on 12 October 2026; the date in brackets is the page's own "Last updated" line):
--   (1) "Apply for Singapore Citizenship"      https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/citizenship/apply             [30 June 2026]
--   (2) "Singapore Citizenship" (landing page) https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/citizenship                   [not recorded]
--   (3) "Oath-taking for Minors"               https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/citizenship/minor-oath-taking [29 June 2026]
--   (4) "Apply for Permanent Residence"        https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/PR/apply                      [13 March 2026]
--   (5) "Apply for Long-Term Visit Pass"       https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/LTVP/apply                    [08 April 2026]
--       and https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/LTVP (the same content)                                          [08 April 2026]
--   (6) LTVP, spouse of a Singapore citizen    https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/LTVP/apply/spouse-of-a-singapore-citizen-(sc)
--                                                                                                          [06 April 2026]
--   (7) Pre-Marriage LTVP Assessment (PMLA)    https://www.ica.gov.sg/reside/PMLA                          [27 October 2025]
--   (8) Renunciation (of SINGAPORE citizenship) https://www.ica.gov.sg/enter-depart/for-singapore-citizens/renunciation
--                                                                                                          [13 March 2026]
--   (9) Document checklist for citizenship     https://www.ica.gov.sg/docs/default-source/ica/ipses/sc-document-checklist
--
-- AS PUBLISHED, NOT LAW. Every figure and test below is administrative policy as ICA states it on its website, not a rule
-- of law. ICA can change any of it without legislation and without notice; the pages give no effective dates, only a "Last
-- updated" date, so each figure is dated by the page it came from (list above) and is good only "as published" on that
-- date and as read on 12 October 2026. No figure here has a dated arm, because no page gives one.
--
-- THE LAW BEHIND THE POLICY, LEFT TO ITS OWN ROWS. Citizenship by registration of a citizen's wife is Art 123(2) of the
-- Constitution, with the oath in Art 126 and renunciation by a Singapore citizen in Art 128 -- encoded in the row
-- subjects/sg/constitution-of-the-republic-of-singapore/encodings/naive-2026-10 (`the spouse may be registered under Article
-- 123(2)`). There the Government "may" register: the grant is discretionary, and nothing here makes it a right. The pass
-- and permanent residence are under the Immigration Act 1959 (s 10 entry permits, s 55(1)(c) passes by regulations),
-- encoded in subjects/sg/immigration-act-1959/encodings/naive-2026-10 (imm-spouse-passes-and-pr.l4). The Immigration
-- Regulations are not deposited. Where the policy and the Constitution differ (Art 123(2) asks for 2 years' residence;
-- ICA asks for 2 years as a PR AND 2 years of marriage) this module states ICA's test and does not decide between them.
--
-- WHY. REQ-0291 (cradle-to-grave-haziq, event h049, 20 July 2033): "The foreign wife of a citizen has been a permanent
-- resident for two years and married for nine. May she be registered as a citizen, and what must she renounce?" Also
-- helps REQ-0286 (event h033, 10 December 2024: the Malaysian spouse's LTVP, then PR), which stays open under the
-- Immigration Regulations.
--
-- WHAT THE PAGES DO NOT SAY. None of the pages read states, for an ADULT applicant, that foreign citizenship must be
-- renounced, or that an oath must be taken; page (1) says only that successful applicants receive an In-Principle Approval
-- and are made citizens once they have "fulfilled the necessary conditions", which it does not list beyond the Singapore
-- Citizenship Journey for ages 16 to 60. Page (8) is about renouncing Singapore citizenship, not a foreign one. The only
-- published mention of foreign renunciation is page (3): for MINORS registered as citizens, the Oath of Renunciation,
-- Allegiance and Loyalty (ORAL) is taken between 21 and 22 and a "Foreign Citizenship Renunciation Certificate" is among
-- its documents. So the second half of REQ-0291 ("what must she renounce?") is NOT answered from ICA's pages.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ICA's assessment factors (family ties, economic contribution, qualifications, age, family profile, length
-- of residence, commitment to sinking roots) -- listed without weights, so they stay with the decision-maker; LTVP+ (page
-- (5) says only, in its page description, that foreign spouses of citizens are "considered for LTVP+" if they meet its
-- requirements, which it does not state); LTVP validity periods (not stated); National Service; the Work Permit holder's
-- need for the Controller of Work Passes' approval before marrying (a Ministry of Manpower rule, page (6)); the other
-- citizenship and PR categories except adult PRs; payment methods; documents.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. One pass, from the pages above, without the writing-l4-rules skill loaded (not available in this
-- session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `ICA's published framework for a citizen's foreign spouse (as published, not law)`

§§ `Citizenship -- page (1)`

-- Page (1), category "spouse of a Singapore citizen": a PR "for at least 2 years" and married to a Singapore citizen "for at
-- least 2 years"; the citizen spouse sponsors the application through ICA e-Service with Singpass.
GIVEN `years as a permanent resident` IS A NUMBER, `years married to a citizen` IS A NUMBER, `sponsored by the citizen spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible to apply for citizenship as a citizen's spouse` IF
        `years as a permanent resident` AT LEAST 2
    AND `years married to a citizen` AT LEAST 2
    AND `sponsored by the citizen spouse`

-- Page (1), the general category: a PR for at least 2 years and aged 21 and above.
GIVEN `years as a permanent resident` IS A NUMBER, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible to apply for citizenship as an adult PR` IF
        `years as a permanent resident` AT LEAST 2
    AND `age` AT LEAST 21

GIVEN `years as a permanent resident` IS A NUMBER, `years married to a citizen` IS A NUMBER, `sponsored by the citizen spouse` IS A BOOLEAN, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible to apply for citizenship on either footing` IF
        `eligible to apply for citizenship as a citizen's spouse` `years as a permanent resident` `years married to a citizen` `sponsored by the citizen spouse`
    OR  `eligible to apply for citizenship as an adult PR` `years as a permanent resident` `age`

-- What eligibility gives. Eligibility is to APPLY; ICA assesses and grants at its discretion (and Art 123(2) says the
-- Government "may" register).
DECLARE PublishedOutcome IS ONE OF
    `may apply; grant at the Government's discretion`
    `not within the published category`

GIVEN `years as a permanent resident` IS A NUMBER, `years married to a citizen` IS A NUMBER, `sponsored by the citizen spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PublishedOutcome
`the published citizenship answer for a citizen's spouse` MEANS
    IF `eligible to apply for citizenship as a citizen's spouse` `years as a permanent resident` `years married to a citizen` `sponsored by the citizen spouse`
    THEN `may apply; grant at the Government's discretion`
    ELSE `not within the published category`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ICA's pages make citizenship a right for an eligible spouse` MEANS FALSE

-- Page (1), completion of formalities: applicants "aged 16 to 60" must complete the Singapore Citizenship Journey.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must complete the Singapore Citizenship Journey` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 16
    AND `age` AT MOST 60

-- Page (1), fees for adult PRs: $100 on submission; on completion $70 for the citizenship certificate and $10 for the
-- identity card for new citizens aged 15 and above.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`citizenship fee at submission` MEANS 100

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`citizenship fee at completion` `age` MEANS
    IF `age` AT LEAST 15 THEN 70 PLUS 10 ELSE 70

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`citizenship fees in all` `age` MEANS
    `citizenship fee at submission` PLUS `citizenship fee at completion` `age`

-- Page (1): applications are processed "within 12 months".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months within which a citizenship application is processed` MEANS 12

§§ `Renunciation and the oath -- what the pages say`

-- No page read states a renunciation or oath requirement for an adult applicant (see the header).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ICA's adult citizenship pages state that foreign citizenship must be renounced` MEANS FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ICA's adult citizenship pages state that an oath must be taken` MEANS FALSE

-- Page (3), minors registered as citizens (by descent or registration): the ORAL is taken "after turning 21 and before
-- their 22nd birthday"; there is no fee; failing it, citizenship is lost on the 22nd birthday; the documents include a
-- Foreign Citizenship Renunciation Certificate.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the window for a minor's ORAL` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `age` LESS THAN 22

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `has taken the ORAL` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a citizen registered as a minor loses citizenship for want of the ORAL` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 22
    AND (NOT `has taken the ORAL`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`fee for the ORAL` MEANS 0

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ORAL documents include a foreign citizenship renunciation certificate` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Permanent residence -- page (4)`

-- Page (4): "Spouse of a Singapore citizen or Singapore permanent resident" may apply, sponsored by the spouse with
-- Singpass. No minimum marriage or residence period is stated.
GIVEN `married to a citizen or PR` IS A BOOLEAN, `sponsored by the spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible to apply for PR as the spouse of a citizen or PR` IF
        `married to a citizen or PR`
    AND `sponsored by the spouse`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ICA's PR page states a minimum period of marriage or residence for a spouse` MEANS FALSE

-- Page (4), fees: $100 on submission; on completion $20 entry permit, $50 five-year re-entry permit, $50 identity card.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`PR fee at submission` MEANS 100

GIVETH A NUMBER
`PR fee at completion` MEANS 20 PLUS 50 PLUS 50

GIVETH A NUMBER
`PR fees in all` MEANS `PR fee at submission` PLUS `PR fee at completion`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`years of the re-entry permit issued with PR` MEANS 5

-- Page (4): processed "within 6 months".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months within which a PR application is processed` MEANS 6

§§ `Long-Term Visit Pass -- pages (5), (6), (7)`

-- Page (5): "Spouse of a Singapore citizen" is an eligible category; the citizen spouse sponsors with Singpass. Page (6):
-- marriage does not guarantee approval.
GIVEN `married to a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `sponsored by the citizen spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible to apply for an LTVP as a citizen's spouse` IF
        `married to a citizen`
    AND `sponsored by the citizen spouse`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`marriage to a citizen guarantees an LTVP` MEANS FALSE

-- Pages (5), (6), fees: $45 on submission; on completion $60 for issue and $30 for a Multiple Journey Visa if applicable.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`LTVP fee at submission` MEANS 45

GIVEN `needs a multiple journey visa` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`LTVP fee at completion` `needs a multiple journey visa` MEANS
    IF `needs a multiple journey visa` THEN 60 PLUS 30 ELSE 60

GIVEN `needs a multiple journey visa` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`LTVP fees in all` `needs a multiple journey visa` MEANS
    `LTVP fee at submission` PLUS `LTVP fee at completion` `needs a multiple journey visa`

-- Pages (5), (6), (7): a foreign spouse's LTVP application takes up to 6 months; 6 weeks if the couple completed the PMLA
-- before marriage.
DECLARE ProcessingTime IS ONE OF
    `within 6 weeks`
    `up to 6 months`

GIVEN `completed the PMLA before marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ProcessingTime
`processing time for a citizen's spouse's LTVP` `completed the PMLA before marriage` MEANS
    IF `completed the PMLA before marriage` THEN `within 6 weeks` ELSE `up to 6 months`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`fee for the PMLA` MEANS 0

-- Page (7): with a positive assessment the couple may apply for the LTVP "within 1 year" of the Letter of Eligibility.
-- Counted here in whole months; the day on which the year ends is not encoded.
GIVEN `months since the letter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the PMLA letter can still be used` IF
        `months since the letter` AT MOST 12

-- Page (5): renew "at least 3 months" before expiry; the renewed pass runs from its date of issue and the remaining
-- validity of the old pass is not carried over.
GIVEN `months before expiry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the LTVP renewal is submitted as ICA asks` IF
        `months before expiry` AT LEAST 3

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`remaining LTVP validity is carried into the renewed pass` MEANS FALSE
